<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 hirashix0

Bundled SMAppService LaunchAgent for the per-user librescrs-agent daemon
(the host app looks this up by basename via
AppGroupConstants.AgentService.launchdPlistName — keep the filename and the
Label in sync with that constant). BundleProgram (NOT ProgramArguments) is
required: SMAppService resolves BundleProgram relative to the enclosing
app bundle, so the staged path stays correct across every install location;
an absolute ProgramArguments path breaks the moment the .app is relocated.
KeepAlive is the respawn mechanism now that there is no PrompterSupervisor
— launchd restarts the agent only after a crash: a non-zero exit, or a
fatal signal it never installed a handler for (SuccessfulExit false). The
agent itself traps SIGTERM/SIGINT, quiesces, and returns 0
(agent/src/main.cpp), so a plain `kill`/`killall` is a CLEAN exit under
that definition, not a crash — it stops the agent for good until the next
login or a `launchctl kickstart`, never an automatic respawn. A future
"Quit agent" action in the host relies on exactly this: it issues that same
clean stop and must `launchctl kickstart` the job itself to bring the
agent back. ThrottleInterval backs off a repeated failure instead of
spinning launchd in a crash loop.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>org.librescrs.agent</string>
    <key>BundleProgram</key>
    <string>Contents/MacOS/librescrs-agent</string>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Interactive</string>
    <key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
    <array>
        <string>org.librescrs.LibreMac</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
